    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d586">

                <pb facs="0567" n="555" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg555"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.20/254a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ford</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-11-11T14:00:00-04:00">November 11,
                            1943—2 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>574. Effective on the date when the <hi rendition="#italic">Gendarmerie</hi>
                    contract is signed, the War Department, with the concurrence of the Department
                    of State, is relieving Colonel Schwarzkopf from assignment to duty with the
                    American Minister at Tehran and assigning him as Chief of the United States Army
                    Mission to Iran in connection with the reorganization of the Iranian <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gendarmerie</hi>.</p>
                <p>Schwarzkopf will discuss this with you on his return.<anchor n="68"
                        xml:id="d586-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d586-f1" n="68" xml:id="d586-f1-content">
                <p>Colonel Schwarzkopf had been in the United States for consultation with the War
                    Department.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
